WEBVTT

00:02.080 --> 00:04.220
Wow, that's adorable!

00:04.220 --> 00:07.110
Knowing Maki, it's hard to believe 
he had a phase like that.

00:07.110 --> 00:09.660
He sure did.

00:09.660 --> 00:15.440
Back then, he'd cling to me, 
going, "Mommy! Mommy!"

00:16.680 --> 00:18.700
I'm starting to picture it now.

00:18.700 --> 00:19.830
What's going on here?

00:20.350 --> 00:21.960
Hey, morning.

00:21.960 --> 00:25.630
I think today will be a wonderful day.

00:25.630 --> 00:26.800
Really, now?

00:26.800 --> 00:30.050
Mine couldn't have begun 
any worse, if you ask me.

00:30.050 --> 00:33.660
I saw all your photos. They were so cute!

00:33.660 --> 00:35.200
Especially the one with your baby...

00:35.200 --> 00:37.140
Don't say a single word more.

00:37.460 --> 00:38.850
I made sure Yuu wouldn't see

00:39.220 --> 00:41.720
by taking out the pictures in question.

00:41.720 --> 00:45.150
Yeah? And where are those pictures now?

00:45.150 --> 00:47.660
Huh? In my bag, of course.

00:47.660 --> 00:49.890
Your mother said it was okay.

00:50.740 --> 00:53.120
Don't try to casually take them with you!

00:53.120 --> 00:55.080
And Mom, don't just agree to it!

02:29.130 --> 02:30.620
Maki? Sorry!

02:30.620 --> 02:35.010
I left my smokes and lighter on the table.
Could you bring them downstairs?

02:35.270 --> 02:36.800
These ones, right? Here.

02:37.140 --> 02:38.270
Thanks.

02:41.190 --> 02:43.270
She has seemed really busy lately,

02:43.850 --> 02:47.440
so I can see why she'd want 
her smoke breaks.

02:47.730 --> 02:50.600
Listen. Just so we're perfectly clear,

02:51.050 --> 02:54.400
don't reveal too much 
of our family situation to Umi-chan.

02:59.400 --> 03:02.170
Don't worry. I get it.

03:02.170 --> 03:02.870
All right.

03:03.270 --> 03:04.970
Time to go put a shift in.

03:05.560 --> 03:07.370
Yeah, take care.

03:11.150 --> 03:12.300
Hey...

03:12.300 --> 03:13.900
Mm? What?

03:15.660 --> 03:17.930
I want to talk about this Friday.

03:17.930 --> 03:21.380
Yeah, that's when our exams start. 
What do you want to do?

03:21.380 --> 03:23.180
We could have dinner 
and do some studying—

03:23.180 --> 03:25.270
I'm going to be meeting 
with my dad that day.

03:27.710 --> 03:30.400
Are you ready for that?

03:31.780 --> 03:33.900
Hey, it's nothing new.

03:34.320 --> 03:37.100
We'll just be getting dinner together.

03:37.100 --> 03:39.150
What about the thing with his subordinate?

03:39.150 --> 03:41.280
I do want to ask him about it.

03:41.580 --> 03:44.620
I wouldn't feel right about 
leaving things as they are.

03:46.120 --> 03:49.750
So I need to hit the books hard 
before I go.

03:49.750 --> 03:52.930
Do we know when everybody's free 
to get together for a study session?

03:52.930 --> 03:57.900
Milady was like, 
"Please! I'd go every day if I could!"

03:57.900 --> 04:01.760
Got it. Let's get started today, then.

04:01.760 --> 04:05.120
Sounds good. I'll let Yuu know.

04:09.830 --> 04:12.720
I'm planning to study with Nozomu.

04:13.180 --> 04:15.800
I guess it's up to Amami-san 
if we all do it as a group.

04:17.780 --> 04:20.570
Sure! I'm totally okay 
with Seki-kun being there.

04:20.570 --> 04:22.910
Huh? You are?

04:22.910 --> 04:25.730
Hey, the more the merrier.

04:25.730 --> 04:27.370
By the way, what will we be snacking on?

04:27.910 --> 04:31.420
There's some pancake batter 
left over from breakfast,

04:31.420 --> 04:34.550
so I was thinking I'd use it up.

04:34.550 --> 04:37.420
Perfect! I can't wait!

04:38.590 --> 04:41.020
You know studying comes first, right,

04:41.020 --> 04:46.060
milady who barely walks the passing line 
and sometimes get stuck doing makeups?

04:46.060 --> 04:49.020
Yes, ma'am!

04:50.200 --> 04:54.120
Yo, you're actually an awesome dude, huh?

04:54.120 --> 04:55.700
You've got my utmost respect.

04:55.700 --> 04:57.030
Y-Yeah?

04:57.550 --> 04:59.600
Are you sure about this?

05:00.390 --> 05:04.050
Should I really be coming along?

05:04.790 --> 05:08.500
Amami-san said it was okay, 
so don't worry about it.

05:09.160 --> 05:13.870
Either way, we're not hanging out for fun. 
Focus on studying...

05:13.870 --> 05:17.460
as much as you can, anyway. 
I know it won't be easy.

05:17.460 --> 05:21.270
You got it. I really don't wanna 
be stuck with any makeups.

05:30.760 --> 05:32.140
By the way...

05:32.510 --> 05:35.760
Where do you usually rank 
on exams, Asanagi?

05:37.420 --> 05:39.420
Single-digits when she's on her game,

05:39.420 --> 05:41.780
and in the teens even when she's not.

05:41.780 --> 05:43.580
Wow.

05:43.580 --> 05:46.610
Why are you getting smug about it, milady?

05:48.600 --> 05:50.600
I'm just proud of my best friend.

05:51.910 --> 05:53.210
And you, Maki?

05:53.690 --> 05:56.860
I'm usually around 50th or thereabouts.

05:56.860 --> 06:03.130
Oh... I'm definitely not gonna be in 
the same class as you two next year.

06:04.470 --> 06:09.350
I hate studying. But I hate the idea of 
being separated from Umi even more.

06:09.350 --> 06:13.420
Then you'd better bust your ass and 
make it into the top half, at least.

06:13.420 --> 06:15.050
Yes, ma'am.

06:16.600 --> 06:18.020
Hey, Maki-kun...

06:18.380 --> 06:21.400
How do I translate this part?

06:21.400 --> 06:23.750
Oh, for that...

06:25.710 --> 06:26.280
Huh?

06:32.020 --> 06:33.960
What's wrong, Maki-kun?

06:33.960 --> 06:36.320
O-Oh, sorry.

06:36.320 --> 06:39.000
The translation for this, right?

06:39.000 --> 06:43.470
Seki, you messed up the calculations 
on the second stage of that equation.

06:43.830 --> 06:46.270
Double-check the brackets.

06:46.270 --> 06:47.970
Huh? Oh...

06:48.290 --> 06:49.930
You're right. My bad.

06:57.660 --> 06:59.860
Let's eat!

07:04.120 --> 07:05.900
Yummy!

07:07.430 --> 07:09.580
Maki, you've got cream on your face.

07:11.980 --> 07:12.940
Did I get it?

07:12.940 --> 07:14.800
Not completely.

07:14.800 --> 07:17.080
Where is it? Left side or right?

07:17.080 --> 07:19.540
Oh, you're hopeless.

07:19.820 --> 07:21.880
Face this way.

07:21.880 --> 07:22.630
Okay.

07:28.620 --> 07:30.260
There, all gone.

07:30.260 --> 07:32.410
Th-Thanks.

07:32.410 --> 07:33.560
You're welcome.

07:33.560 --> 07:36.520
You're such a baby, Maki.

07:36.520 --> 07:39.420
This doesn't happen all the time, okay?

07:39.420 --> 07:40.480
Whatever you say.

07:40.950 --> 07:42.730
Umi? Maki-kun?

07:44.760 --> 07:50.970
You guys are basically going out, 
so we get it. Nobody's gonna complain.

07:51.440 --> 07:55.620
But save it for when 
you're alone, will you?

07:57.170 --> 07:59.180
Sorry.

07:59.180 --> 08:02.630
I'm so envious of your 
relationship, though.

08:02.630 --> 08:08.050
Man, I wish I had a guy 
like Maki-kun in my life, too.

08:09.340 --> 08:13.460
He's nice, and he makes snacks 
when we hang out.

08:13.460 --> 08:17.610
You'd be better off with a guy with 
maxed-out stats, especially stamina.

08:17.610 --> 08:21.000
Nobody else could keep up 
with your endless energy.

08:21.000 --> 08:26.440
You think? But where am I going 
to find someone like that...

08:26.700 --> 08:27.400
Hey!

08:27.400 --> 08:29.780
Someone like you!

08:30.090 --> 08:32.740
That means cloning you 
will solve everything!

08:32.740 --> 08:34.360
Good luck with that!

08:36.520 --> 08:39.580
Thanks for tutoring us, Maki-kun.

08:39.580 --> 08:41.700
The snacks were great, too.

08:41.700 --> 08:45.130
Thanks to you, I'm starting 
to think I can pull through.

08:45.460 --> 08:48.240
We gotta make sure 
not to fail any subjects, Seki-kun.

08:48.240 --> 08:49.840
Let's do this!

08:50.180 --> 08:55.310
Y-Yeah. You try not to fail 
any too, Amami-san.

08:55.310 --> 08:58.530
Oh, I need to talk to Maki 
about something.

08:58.530 --> 09:00.560
Can you wait for me by the entrance?

09:01.820 --> 09:02.860
Okay.

09:02.860 --> 09:04.660
See you tomorrow.

09:07.460 --> 09:09.360
Umi? Talk about what?

09:12.860 --> 09:13.720
Umi?

09:14.230 --> 09:16.340
I'm really sorry, okay?

09:17.280 --> 09:21.210
I know I'm being kind of a pain.

09:21.540 --> 09:24.740
But I just got a little bit worried.

09:24.740 --> 09:26.670
Did something happen today?

09:27.380 --> 09:31.880
You heard what Yuu said. 
"A guy like Maki-kun."

09:31.880 --> 09:33.890
Oh, that?

09:34.530 --> 09:37.440
I can't take it, okay?

09:38.000 --> 09:41.550
I managed to get over 
the Sanae and Manaka thing...

09:42.240 --> 09:48.350
But if I lose you, I'm sure 
I'll be traumatized for life.

09:49.150 --> 09:50.070
Umi.

09:51.130 --> 09:53.360
Could you let me go for a sec?

09:53.360 --> 09:57.090
No. I don't want you seeing 
the state my face is in right now.

09:57.090 --> 09:58.400
It won't bother me.

09:58.900 --> 10:02.360
I've seen you cry before.

10:03.630 --> 10:05.040
You jerk.

10:05.920 --> 10:07.420
Don't worry.

10:08.270 --> 10:11.090
I only have eyes for you.

10:14.180 --> 10:18.140
Thanks. That helped me feel better.

10:18.390 --> 10:20.150
Glad to hear it.

10:20.150 --> 10:22.300
Do you want me to walk you home?

10:22.300 --> 10:26.690
I'm not going to ask 
that much of you. But...

10:29.230 --> 10:32.360
I do want to stay like this a bit longer.

10:34.410 --> 10:35.530
Do you mind?

10:36.000 --> 10:38.450
N-Not really.

10:38.790 --> 10:39.760
Thanks.

10:49.880 --> 10:51.920
TODAY
MAKI, ARE YOU SURE YOU'LL BE OKAY TONIGHT?

10:51.920 --> 10:55.430
I KNOW I'M BEING A BUSYBODY,
BUT I CAN AT LEAST GO THERE WITH YOU.

10:55.430 --> 10:57.550
I'LL BE OKAY. DON'T WORRY. I'M JUST
GOING TO STUFF MY FACE AT A DINER.

11:01.130 --> 11:06.600
MAYBE I SHOULD GO. YOU'RE GOING
TO THAT KINDA FANCY PLACE, RIGHT?

11:01.370 --> 11:03.730
You're going to that 
kinda fancy place, right?

11:03.730 --> 11:06.610
It's got that expensive 
A5 wagyu fillet steak

11:06.610 --> 11:09.300
and fried tiger-shrimp combo 
with an extra-large rice

11:09.300 --> 11:11.760
and a loaded strawberry 
parfait for dessert!

11:11.760 --> 11:15.270
Ah, interesting. 
Guess I know what I'm ordering.

11:15.990 --> 11:19.520
Damn it! I'm so jealous 
you get to eat for free!

11:20.530 --> 11:21.870
Once I'm done...

11:21.870 --> 11:24.320
I'll message you right away, okay?

11:25.560 --> 11:27.080
Sorry, Maki.

11:27.640 --> 11:29.000
I kept you waiting.

11:30.790 --> 11:33.840
I'm starving. Shall we start by ordering?

11:34.560 --> 11:36.220
What'll you have, Maki?

11:37.210 --> 11:41.300
The A5 wagyu fillet steak 
and fried tiger-shrimp combo

11:41.600 --> 11:43.270
with an extra-large rice

11:43.270 --> 11:46.690
and a loaded strawberry 
parfait for dessert.

11:46.690 --> 11:50.020
Whoa. You're going to town.

11:50.480 --> 11:52.510
You used to hold back in the past.

11:52.510 --> 11:53.980
Hey, we haven't had dinner in a while.

11:53.980 --> 11:58.400
All right. I'll join you 
and stuff my face for once.

12:00.670 --> 12:04.160
Dad, can I ask you something?

12:04.540 --> 12:05.440
Hm?

12:06.220 --> 12:08.920
Do you still love Mom?

12:09.530 --> 12:11.790
Where'd this come from?

12:11.790 --> 12:15.320
Nowhere. I'm just curious.

12:15.960 --> 12:17.470
I can't be sure,

12:18.550 --> 12:21.090
but I don't think I feel that way anymore.

12:22.820 --> 12:23.790
Oh.

12:24.750 --> 12:29.310
She was an amazing wife and 
mother for so many years,

12:29.740 --> 12:32.240
so obviously I respect her 
a lot as a person.

12:34.030 --> 12:36.410
That's never going to change.

12:37.040 --> 12:40.920
But could I call her family again? 
That's a whole different matter.

12:41.410 --> 12:43.300
What if I was part of the deal?

12:44.330 --> 12:46.950
Again, it'd be different 
if it was just you.

12:47.540 --> 12:52.210
Even during the divorce, we fought 
over your custody until the bitter end.

12:54.070 --> 12:58.840
They both love me and care about me. 
They always have and always will.

12:59.880 --> 13:03.520
And yet, Dad and Mom 
chose to get a divorce.

13:04.870 --> 13:08.080
I guess that goes to show 
how much they grew apart.

13:10.160 --> 13:12.970
Did you fall out of love with Mom...

13:14.230 --> 13:15.730
because of Minato-san?

13:19.410 --> 13:22.280
So you did see us the other night.

13:22.630 --> 13:23.990
You knew I was there?

13:25.400 --> 13:26.920
Of course I did.

13:26.920 --> 13:31.330
No matter how much you dress up and 
change your look, you'll always be my boy.

13:31.650 --> 13:33.800
Was that girl a friend?

13:34.210 --> 13:38.050
Yeah... We became friends 
a little while ago.

13:38.580 --> 13:42.000
But putting that aside, what's the story 
between you and Minato-san?

13:42.410 --> 13:44.730
You two seemed awfully close.

13:44.730 --> 13:47.880
Wait, did you get the idea 
that I was cheating?

13:48.700 --> 13:52.900
I swear to you, we only started 
meeting outside of work

13:52.900 --> 13:55.810
long after your mother and I divorced.

13:55.810 --> 13:58.400
Do you love Minato-san?

13:59.920 --> 14:05.070
She does work for me. 
She knows everything I go through.

14:05.970 --> 14:08.540
She's being a massive help to me.

14:14.270 --> 14:16.710
You love her, huh?

14:19.570 --> 14:21.580
You're free to think that.

14:21.580 --> 14:23.000
Do you not love her?

14:24.230 --> 14:27.050
I do... love her.

14:31.340 --> 14:32.230
Maki.

14:32.740 --> 14:35.940
I noticed this last time, 
but you've got dishpan hands.

14:37.080 --> 14:40.420
Remember to use some 
hand cream before bed.

14:40.420 --> 14:41.700
Wha?

14:41.700 --> 14:45.240
Forgive me. I'd like to spend more time 
with you, but I need to go.

14:45.240 --> 14:46.780
Hang on. I'm not done—

14:46.780 --> 14:48.660
Wha? What are you even saying?

14:48.660 --> 14:50.330
I can't believe you!

14:50.750 --> 14:52.110
Nitta-san?

14:52.110 --> 14:52.930
Huh?

14:53.330 --> 14:56.000
Ack! C-Class rep?

14:56.290 --> 14:57.420
A friend of yours?

14:57.420 --> 14:58.750
Y-Yeah.

14:59.180 --> 15:03.790
What's wrong, Nitta-san? 
What's got you yelling?

15:03.790 --> 15:04.970
Oh, uh...

15:05.750 --> 15:08.230
I'm kind of in a pickle.

15:09.010 --> 15:11.930
Financially, I mean.

15:11.930 --> 15:14.820
Wait, you don't have enough?

15:14.820 --> 15:17.770
Uh, well...

15:18.890 --> 15:19.990
Yeah.

15:21.460 --> 15:25.490
I was actually here to see my boyfriend.

15:25.490 --> 15:28.320
He told me to go ahead 
and eat while I waited,

15:28.780 --> 15:30.830
and that he'd pay for it.

15:31.150 --> 15:34.510
But he called me just now, and...

15:35.150 --> 15:37.960
He can't make it, and he's not paying up?

15:38.220 --> 15:41.590
He's not coming because 
he landed a date with his #1 target!

15:42.070 --> 15:43.380
Ah...

15:43.700 --> 15:49.110
The thing is, even if 
I overlook that, which I can't...

15:49.110 --> 15:52.100
I only have a little over 1,000 yen on me.

15:52.690 --> 15:54.450
How much are you short?

15:55.060 --> 15:58.060
Huh? Oh, uh...

15:58.060 --> 16:00.840
I think by around 2,000 yen or so.

16:00.840 --> 16:01.900
You are...

16:02.250 --> 16:06.890
I'm Maehara Itsuki. I appreciate 
you being friends with my son.

16:06.890 --> 16:07.930
You're the class rep—

16:08.320 --> 16:12.430
Maehara-kun's dad? 
Oh, no, the pleasure is all mine.

16:12.430 --> 16:14.120
Wait, you'll pay for her?

16:14.120 --> 16:17.680
I wouldn't do it for just anybody, 
but she's my son's classmate.

16:17.680 --> 16:20.310
I can't very well overlook her 
if she's in trouble.

16:21.000 --> 16:26.240
B-But I couldn't possibly ask that of you.

16:28.800 --> 16:32.970
Don't. She's my friend, 
so I'll pay for her.

16:32.970 --> 16:34.120
Maki?

16:34.670 --> 16:37.310
You're not family anymore, right?

16:37.310 --> 16:39.600
Quit trying to act like it, then.

16:39.910 --> 16:41.720
Let's go, Nitta-san.

16:43.120 --> 16:44.240
You sure?

16:46.560 --> 16:49.920
Dad, can I ask you one last thing?

16:50.660 --> 16:51.700
What is it?

16:51.700 --> 16:54.320
Do you love Minato-san?

16:57.490 --> 17:00.340
One day, you'll understand.

17:00.710 --> 17:03.960
If that's your answer, 
then I get it already.

17:04.470 --> 17:05.340
Bye.

17:15.570 --> 17:17.890
Hey, can we stop by the convenience store?

17:18.300 --> 17:22.010
I could use some coffee, 
since it's so cold out.

17:22.010 --> 17:24.700
And I'm paying for that, too?

17:24.700 --> 17:28.650
Relax. I'll pay it all back.

17:29.110 --> 17:30.130
Sheesh.

17:30.590 --> 17:32.620
Just one coffee, okay?

17:32.620 --> 17:34.340
Cheers!

17:37.040 --> 17:39.860
I feel so much better now.

17:40.820 --> 17:46.040
You never had any friends 
until Asanagi, did you?

17:46.970 --> 17:50.380
We kept moving because of my dad's work.

17:51.100 --> 17:52.970
And you know how I am.

17:52.970 --> 17:57.230
I knew a kid like that 
back in elementary school, too.

17:57.230 --> 18:01.770
I'd always think that it couldn't 
be that hard to make friends.

18:02.790 --> 18:04.860
But now I get that it's complicated.

18:11.150 --> 18:14.820
24H CONVENIENCE

18:12.150 --> 18:14.820
I know this isn't the time 
or place to ask,

18:15.360 --> 18:17.130
but do your parents get along?

18:17.760 --> 18:20.070
They don't not get along.

18:20.070 --> 18:24.300
Though whenever they're in the same room, 
objects start to fly around everywhere.

18:24.300 --> 18:26.170
Can you really say 
they get along like that?

18:26.490 --> 18:29.300
I mean, yeah, they fight.

18:29.300 --> 18:31.860
But they always make up the same day,

18:31.860 --> 18:34.540
and at night I start to hear 
the bed creak and some moaning.

18:34.540 --> 18:37.340
You really didn't have to share that part.

18:39.090 --> 18:45.000
When you're family, the annoyances 
inevitably start piling up.

18:45.420 --> 18:49.740
Like how I don't study enough, 
or money or work issues.

18:50.410 --> 18:54.320
I've kinda developed a radar for that.

18:54.320 --> 18:59.990
I can tell if they're still piling up, 
or if they're going to explode soon.

18:59.990 --> 19:01.370
I can see it on their faces.

19:03.770 --> 19:06.340
Could you tell with me and my dad, too?

19:06.340 --> 19:10.220
Yeah, but in your dad's case,

19:10.220 --> 19:14.550
it's more like his bomb was a dud.

19:15.050 --> 19:20.400
He missed his chance to explode, 
and now it's all too late for everything.

19:21.050 --> 19:24.660
Anyway, forget about your dad.

19:24.660 --> 19:27.850
The one that has my alarm bells 
ringing is you, class rep.

19:28.120 --> 19:29.120
Wait, me?

19:29.120 --> 19:33.670
Yes, you. You're acting 
like you're above it all,

19:33.670 --> 19:36.990
but you're close to ending up a dud, too.

19:38.060 --> 19:41.450
Just like my dad?

19:41.450 --> 19:42.700
COMBUSTIBLE

19:43.190 --> 19:46.870
If you need it, get Asanagi to clean 
your pipes, if you know what I mean.

19:47.320 --> 19:50.660
You might end up going crazy otherwise.

19:50.660 --> 19:52.000
Don't make it sound dirty.

19:52.630 --> 19:54.780
If you go out of whack,

19:54.780 --> 19:58.720
it'll make Asanagi and 
Yuu-chin all gloomy, too.

19:59.120 --> 20:03.620
You're whatever, 
but I care a lot about those two.

20:03.620 --> 20:04.470
Okay.

20:04.910 --> 20:08.020
I'll call Umi now. 
She's probably worried about me.

20:08.360 --> 20:09.550
You do that.

20:10.070 --> 20:12.480
Anyway, thanks for today. See ya.

20:15.430 --> 20:17.070
Morning, Mom.

20:17.640 --> 20:19.830
Isn't it past the time 
you usually head out?

20:19.830 --> 20:23.720
I've been leaving you 
to do all the housework lately.

20:24.220 --> 20:27.540
I've got to be a mom sometimes, you know?

20:28.920 --> 20:30.360
Listen, Maki...

20:31.620 --> 20:35.130
I'm going to be taking some time off work.

20:35.130 --> 20:36.220
What?

20:36.220 --> 20:38.600
At least a couple of months, for starters.

20:39.150 --> 20:42.420
After that, I don't know. 
I'm still considering my options.

20:42.420 --> 20:44.100
Is something wrong with you?

20:44.720 --> 20:47.480
Nah, I'm perfectly healthy.

20:48.230 --> 20:52.060
But if I'd kept going, I would've 
definitely broken down at some point.

20:52.450 --> 20:55.250
I figured I needed to rethink 
my work and lifestyle.

20:58.790 --> 21:01.960
And cut down on your smoking, too.

21:03.730 --> 21:09.620
Yeah? It's cool that she can just decide 
to take a break like that.

21:10.230 --> 21:14.910
But if she's home, that'll mean 
our Friday routine will have to change.

21:15.520 --> 21:17.710
You said it.

21:17.710 --> 21:20.300
What do you want to do this week?

21:20.300 --> 21:22.600
We can hang out at my place like usual,

21:22.600 --> 21:25.640
or we can change things up 
and try something new.

21:26.350 --> 21:28.600
About that...

21:29.760 --> 21:30.810
What's up?

21:31.680 --> 21:37.400
Do you want to come over 
for dinner this Friday?

21:37.660 --> 21:38.400
Huh?

21:38.700 --> 21:41.770
My dear mother's suggestion.

21:41.770 --> 21:44.740
The man of the house 
will be joining us that night.

21:44.740 --> 21:45.700
Not happening.

21:45.700 --> 21:47.380
Don't give me that.

21:47.380 --> 21:51.730
My dad said he wants 
to get a good look at your face.

21:51.730 --> 21:52.220
Nope!

21:52.220 --> 21:54.160
I said, don't give me that!

21:55.650 --> 22:01.170
And so, everything weighing on my mind 
was blown into the ether...

22:01.690 --> 22:04.850
by this special event 
right before Christmas.

